{
  "courseSlug": "understanding-startup-equity-valuation-and-cap-tables-for-investors",
  "chapters": [
    {
      "title": "Chapter 4: Dilution, Down Rounds and Protecting Your Stake",
      "lessons": [
        {
          "title": "Down Rounds and Anti-Dilution: Full Ratchet vs Weighted Average",
          "slug": "down-rounds-and-anti-dilution-full-ratchet-vs-weighted-average",
          "body": [
            {
              "_key": "k1",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k2",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Every dilution example so far has had a happy ending: smaller slice, bigger cake. Now the cake shrinks. A startup that raised at ₹500 per share runs short of cash during a funding winter and the only investor willing to write a cheque offers ₹250. Everyone gets diluted, and the value of every existing share is marked down by half. But not everyone is hurt equally. Investors with anti-dilution protection get extra shares, and those shares come out of everyone else. This lesson shows exactly how, using the two formulas you will see in Indian term sheets.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_type": "bigIdea",
              "text": "Anti-dilution protection does not stop a down round from happening. It decides who pays for it. Every extra share handed to a protected investor comes out of the founders, the ESOP pool and unprotected holders, often including small angels.",
              "_key": "k3"
            },
            {
              "_key": "k4",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k5",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "What a Down Round Is",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_key": "k6",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k7",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "A ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k9",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "down round",
                  "marks": [
                    "k8"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k10",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": " is a round priced lower per share than the one before. In India, down rounds became far more common during the 2022 to 2023 funding winter, when companies that had raised at 2021 valuations needed cash and found investors unwilling to pay those prices.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": [
                {
                  "_key": "k8",
                  "_type": "glossaryTerm",
                  "definition": "A funding round priced lower per share than the previous round."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "_type": "keyFact",
              "label": "A high-profile Indian example",
              "value": "Roughly 90% below the peak",
              "context": "In 2023, PharmEasy's parent raised about ₹3,500 crore through a rights issue at a valuation reported to be roughly 90% below its 2021 peak. Existing shareholders who did not put in more money saw their stakes diluted sharply.",
              "_key": "k11"
            },
            {
              "_type": "statGrid",
              "stats": [
                {
                  "_key": "k13",
                  "label": "Headline valuation",
                  "value": "Falls",
                  "context": "Pre-money below the last post-money"
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k15",
                  "label": "Price per share",
                  "value": "Falls",
                  "context": "The defining feature of a down round"
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k17",
                  "label": "Dilution",
                  "value": "Larger",
                  "context": "Same cash buys more shares at a lower price"
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k19",
                  "label": "Protected investors",
                  "value": "Get extra shares",
                  "context": "Through an adjusted conversion ratio"
                }
              ],
              "_key": "k20"
            },
            {
              "_key": "k21",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k22",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "How Anti-Dilution Works in India",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_key": "k23",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k24",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "In Indian venture deals, anti-dilution protection sits in the terms of an investor's CCPS. The investor paid an original issue price per CCPS, and each CCPS converts at a ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k26",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "conversion price",
                  "marks": [
                    "k25"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k27",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": ". At issue, the conversion price equals the issue price, so each CCPS converts 1:1. If a down round triggers anti-dilution, the conversion price is cut, and each CCPS converts into more equity shares.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": [
                {
                  "_key": "k25",
                  "_type": "glossaryTerm",
                  "definition": "The price at which a CCPS converts into equity shares. The number of equity shares per CCPS equals the original issue price divided by the conversion price."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "_type": "mathBlock",
              "latex": "\\text{Equity shares per CCPS} = \\frac{\\text{Original issue price}}{\\text{Adjusted conversion price}}",
              "caption": "Cut the conversion price and the conversion ratio rises",
              "_key": "k28"
            },
            {
              "_key": "k29",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k30",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "There are two main formulas for cutting that conversion price: full ratchet and weighted average.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_key": "k31",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k32",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Worked Example: PedalPower Hits a Funding Winter",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_key": "k33",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k34",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "PedalPower Mobility Private Limited is a fictional Bengaluru startup renting e-bikes to delivery riders. After its Series A, its fully diluted cap table looks like this.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_type": "table",
              "caption": "PedalPower after Series A (illustrative)",
              "headers": [
                "Holder",
                "Security",
                "Shares",
                "Price paid"
              ],
              "rows": [
                {
                  "_key": "k36",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "Founders",
                    "Equity",
                    "9,00,000",
                    "Face value"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k38",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "ESOP pool",
                    "Options",
                    "1,50,000",
                    "n/a"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k40",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "Seed investors",
                    "Seed CCPS",
                    "1,50,000",
                    "₹200"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k42",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "Series A fund",
                    "Series A CCPS with anti-dilution",
                    "3,00,000",
                    "₹500 (₹15 crore)"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k44",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "Total",
                    "",
                    "15,00,000",
                    ""
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "_key": "k45"
            },
            {
              "_key": "k46",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k47",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "The Series A post-money valuation was 15,00,000 × ₹500 = ₹75 crore. Two years later, PedalPower raises ₹10 crore in a Series B at ₹250 per share, a pre-money valuation of ₹37.5 crore. The Series B investor receives 4,00,000 CCPS.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_type": "callout",
              "type": "insight",
              "text": "The seed investors paid ₹200, below the new ₹250 price. A down round only triggers anti-dilution for investors whose price is above the new round price, so in this example only the Series A fund is affected.",
              "_key": "k48"
            },
            {
              "_key": "k49",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "h3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k50",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Option 1: Full ratchet",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_key": "k51",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k52",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Under ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k54",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "full ratchet",
                  "marks": [
                    "k53"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k55",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": ", the Series A conversion price drops straight to ₹250, the new round price. It does not matter whether the down round raises ₹10 crore or ₹10 lakh.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": [
                {
                  "_key": "k53",
                  "_type": "glossaryTerm",
                  "definition": "An anti-dilution formula that cuts the protected investor's conversion price all the way down to the new, lower round price, regardless of how much money is raised."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "_key": "k56",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k57",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Adjusted conversion price: ₹250",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": [],
              "listItem": "bullet",
              "level": 1
            },
            {
              "_key": "k58",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k59",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Equity shares on conversion: ₹15 crore ÷ ₹250 = 6,00,000",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": [],
              "listItem": "bullet",
              "level": 1
            },
            {
              "_key": "k60",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k61",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Extra shares for the Series A fund: 3,00,000",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": [],
              "listItem": "bullet",
              "level": 1
            },
            {
              "_key": "k62",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "h3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k63",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Option 2: Broad-based weighted average",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_key": "k64",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k65",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "The ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k67",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "broad-based weighted average",
                  "marks": [
                    "k66"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k68",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": " formula cuts the conversion price by an amount that depends on how big the down round is relative to the whole company.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": [
                {
                  "_key": "k66",
                  "_type": "glossaryTerm",
                  "definition": "An anti-dilution formula that reduces the conversion price in proportion to how much money is raised at the lower price and how many shares already exist, counted on a fully diluted basis."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "_type": "mathBlock",
              "latex": "CP_2 = CP_1 \\times \\frac{A + B}{A + C}",
              "caption": "The weighted average formula",
              "_key": "k69"
            },
            {
              "_type": "table",
              "caption": "What each letter means, with PedalPower numbers",
              "headers": [
                "Symbol",
                "Meaning",
                "PedalPower value"
              ],
              "rows": [
                {
                  "_key": "k71",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "CP₁",
                    "Conversion price before the down round",
                    "₹500"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k73",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "A",
                    "Shares outstanding before the round (broad-based: fully diluted)",
                    "15,00,000"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k75",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "B",
                    "Shares the new money would have bought at CP₁",
                    "₹10 crore ÷ ₹500 = 2,00,000"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k77",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "C",
                    "Shares actually issued in the down round",
                    "4,00,000"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k79",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "CP₂",
                    "Adjusted conversion price",
                    "₹500 × 17,00,000 ÷ 19,00,000 = ₹447.37"
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "_key": "k80"
            },
            {
              "_key": "k81",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k82",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Adjusted conversion price: ₹447.37",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": [],
              "listItem": "bullet",
              "level": 1
            },
            {
              "_key": "k83",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k84",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Equity shares on conversion: ₹15 crore ÷ ₹447.37 = 3,35,294",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": [],
              "listItem": "bullet",
              "level": 1
            },
            {
              "_key": "k85",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k86",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Extra shares for the Series A fund: 35,294",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": [],
              "listItem": "bullet",
              "level": 1
            },
            {
              "_key": "k87",
              "_type": "collapsible",
              "title": "Narrow-based weighted average: the middle ground",
              "content": [
                {
                  "_key": "k88",
                  "_type": "block",
                  "style": "normal",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "_key": "k89",
                      "_type": "span",
                      "text": "A narrow-based version uses the same formula but counts only a narrower group of shares in A, often just the outstanding preference shares. A smaller A makes the adjustment bigger.",
                      "marks": []
                    }
                  ],
                  "markDefs": []
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k90",
                  "_type": "block",
                  "style": "normal",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "_key": "k91",
                      "_type": "span",
                      "text": "A = Seed CCPS + Series A CCPS = 4,50,000",
                      "marks": []
                    }
                  ],
                  "markDefs": [],
                  "listItem": "bullet",
                  "level": 1
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k92",
                  "_type": "block",
                  "style": "normal",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "_key": "k93",
                      "_type": "span",
                      "text": "CP₂ = ₹500 × (4,50,000 + 2,00,000) ÷ (4,50,000 + 4,00,000) = ₹382.35",
                      "marks": []
                    }
                  ],
                  "markDefs": [],
                  "listItem": "bullet",
                  "level": 1
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k94",
                  "_type": "block",
                  "style": "normal",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "_key": "k95",
                      "_type": "span",
                      "text": "Equity shares on conversion: ₹15 crore ÷ ₹382.35 = 3,92,307",
                      "marks": []
                    }
                  ],
                  "markDefs": [],
                  "listItem": "bullet",
                  "level": 1
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k96",
                  "_type": "block",
                  "style": "normal",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "_key": "k97",
                      "_type": "span",
                      "text": "Extra shares for the Series A fund: 92,307",
                      "marks": []
                    }
                  ],
                  "markDefs": [],
                  "listItem": "bullet",
                  "level": 1
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k98",
                  "_type": "block",
                  "style": "normal",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "_key": "k99",
                      "_type": "span",
                      "text": "Narrow-based protection sits between broad-based and full ratchet, and is less common in balanced term sheets.",
                      "marks": []
                    }
                  ],
                  "markDefs": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "_key": "k100",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "h2",
