              "title": "FEMA limits anti-dilution for foreign investors",
              "content": [
                {
                  "_key": "k148",
                  "_type": "block",
                  "style": "normal",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "_key": "k149",
                      "_type": "span",
                      "text": "Under FEMA pricing rules, CCPS issued to a non-resident cannot convert at a price below the fair value determined when they were issued. If a Singapore fund paid ₹500 per CCPS and the certified fair value at that time was ₹480, the conversion price generally cannot be cut below ₹480, however deep the down round.",
                      "marks": []
                    }
                  ],
                  "markDefs": []
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k150",
                  "_type": "block",
                  "style": "normal",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "_key": "k151",
                      "_type": "span",
                      "text": "Lawyers use various structures to address this, such as founders transferring some of their own shares to the investor, but each has its own pricing, tax and regulatory constraints. The practical takeaway: anti-dilution protection for a foreign investor in an Indian company is often weaker than the term sheet suggests.",
                      "marks": []
                    }
                  ],
                  "markDefs": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "_key": "k152",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k153",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Almost every anti-dilution clause excludes certain share issues, called carve-outs, so that routine events do not trigger an adjustment.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_key": "k154",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k155",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "ESOP grants and exercises",
                  "marks": [
                    "strong"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k156",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": " within the approved pool.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": [],
              "listItem": "bullet",
              "level": 1
            },
            {
              "_key": "k157",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k158",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Conversion of existing CCPS, notes or iSAFEs.",
