            {
              "_type": "callout",
              "type": "insight",
              "text": "Some term sheets add a pay-to-play clause: an investor keeps its anti-dilution protection only if it invests its pro-rata share in the down round. It stops protected investors from sitting back and collecting extra shares while others provide the rescue money.",
